# The platform uses Cloudflare D1 (DB binding in wrangler.jsonc).
# No upstream model key is persisted in browser storage or the database.
# API clients send their provider key for each /v1 request; optional Ask AI
# keeps a user-supplied key in page memory and forwards it per request.
# Email/password works without optional OAuth configuration.
# Google OIDC is enabled only when all three server bindings are configured.
# For local Wrangler development, copy this file to ignored platform/.dev.vars.
# Production: store GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET as a Cloudflare Worker secret.
# Never prefix these with VITE_, expose the secret to the browser, or commit it.
# The redirect URI must exactly match the Web application's registered callback.
# See docs/GOOGLE_AUTH.md; leave blank to keep Google unavailable locally.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=""

# Optional GitHub OAuth login. Use your own app with read:user user:email only.
# Exact callback: https://YOUR_DEPLOYMENT/api/auth/github/callback
# Store all three as server bindings; keep the client secret out of VITE_ and Git.
# See docs/GITHUB_AUTH.md. Blank values keep GitHub unavailable locally.
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=""
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=""
GITHUB_REDIRECT_URI=""
